      { type: "h2", text: "What we do not use" },
      { type: "ul", items: ["We do not invent a \`contentHash\` field. Some adjacent projects use a content hash to authenticate passage quotations, but this repository's evidence schema does not include that field. SHA-256 digests in this repo are reserved for build artifact integrity (\`checksums.sha256\`) and are not used to authenticate evidence passages.", "We do not infer a quote from training data. The model that drafts the page may propose a quote, but a human reviewer must verify the quote against the fetched source before publication.", "We do not fabricate source URLs to satisfy an evidence gate. When a primary source is unavailable, the claim is either removed or reclassified as unresolved."] },
