  "editorial-methodology": {
    title: "Editorial Methodology — How BestAIAgent.in Reviews, Scores, and Publishes",
    description: "How BestAIAgent.in authors, reviews, and publishes AI agent content: editorial independence, source hierarchy, corrections, and author identification.",
    blocks: [
      { type: "p", text: "BestAIAgent.in publishes entity and topic authority content about AI agents for Indian developers, startups, enterprises, and regulated organizations. This page documents how we decide what to publish, what we refuse to publish, who is responsible for each page, and how we correct mistakes." },
      { type: "h2", text: "What this page covers" },
      { type: "ul", items: ["Editorial independence and affiliate disclosure", "Source hierarchy and authority classification", "Page classes and their review requirements", "Author and reviewer identification policy", "Corrections and version history", "When we will not publish a page"] },
      { type: "h2", text: "Editorial independence" },
      { type: "p", text: "BestAIAgent.in is editorially independent. Vendor relationships, affiliate programs, and commercial partnerships do not determine which products we cover, the order in which we cover them, the verdicts we reach, or the framing of any review. Affiliate disclosure is published at [](/trust/affiliate-disclosure) and on every page that links to a commercial partner." },
      { type: "p", text: "We pay for our own product evaluations whenever feasible. Where a vendor provides a temporary licence for testing, we disclose that fact on the affected review page in the \"How we tested\" section." },
      { type: "h2", text: "Source hierarchy" },
      { type: "p", text: "We classify sources by authority before assigning evidence class:" },
      { type: "table", rows: [["Class", "Definition", "Examples"], ["**Primary**", "Vendor / official / statutory source that originates the claim", "Vendor pricing pages, official protocol specifications, statutes, official repositories"], ["**Secondary**", "Independent reporting, peer-reviewed research, official testing bodies", "Reputable technology publications, standards bodies, conference papers"], ["**Community**", "Anecdotal or community-supplied", "Forum threads, blog posts, conference talks without published proceedings"]] },
      { type: "p", text: "For any material claim about price, capability, compliance, or compatibility we require at least one primary source. Comparison pages require equivalent primary sources for both products under review. Legal, medical, financial, and security claims require multiple authoritative sources plus human review — see [](/trust/comparison-methodology) and the relevant methodology pages." },
      { type: "h2", text: "Page classes and review requirements" },
      { type: "p", text: "We use the following page classes. The review depth depends on the risk of the claim being wrong." },
      { type: "ul", items: ["**Pillar** — synthesizes a domain. Requires primary-source evidence for every material claim and editorial review before publication.", "**Cluster** — addresses a specific question inside a pillar. Requires primary-source evidence and editorial review.", "**Comparison** — head-to-head product review. Requires equivalent evidence windows for both products. See [](/trust/comparison-methodology).", "**Review** — single-product review. Requires a tested or desk-researched evaluation method declared up front.", "**Pricing** — current vendor pricing. Requires primary-source evidence and a freshness window. See [](/trust/freshness-policy).", "**Methodology** — this page and its siblings. Reviewed before publication and re-reviewed when underlying policy changes."] },
      { type: "h2", text: "Author and reviewer identification" },
      { type: "p", text: "Every published page identifies the author (where named) and the reviewer (always named). We publish corrections when material errors are identified, even if the page has aged off the homepage. The corrections log lives at [](/trust/corrections)." },
      { type: "h2", text: "When we will not publish a page" },
      { type: "p", text: "We refuse to publish pages when:" },
      { type: "ul", items: ["The page exists primarily to rank for a keyword rather than answer a real user question.", "The required evidence is not available from a primary source.", "The vendor refuses to confirm or deny a claim that materially affects the user's decision.", "The page duplicates an existing page with only reordered adjectives.", "The page would require us to certify a vendor's compliance or security without access to verifiable evidence."] },
      { type: "p", text: "We quarantine such pages as \`quarantined_template\` rather than delete them, so the candidate inventory is auditable." },
      { type: "h2", text: "Related methodology pages" },
      { type: "ul", items: ["[Evidence methodology](/trust/evidence-methodology)", "[Rating methodology](/trust/rating-methodology)", "[Comparison methodology](/trust/comparison-methodology)", "[Source classification](/trust/source-classification)", "[Corrections and version history](/trust/corrections)", "[Freshness policy](/trust/freshness-policy)", "[Affiliate disclosure](/trust/affiliate-disclosure)", "[Author / reviewer policy](/trust/author-reviewer-policy)", "[Privacy and DPDP editorial policy](/trust/privacy-dpdp-editorial-policy)"] },
      { type: "h2", text: "Source receipts" },
      { type: "ul", items: ["Anthropic — Claude's Constitution (primary, retrieved 2026-08-22). Cited for the principle that model behaviour is constrained by documented principles rather than inferred.", "OpenAI — Function Calling documentation (primary, retrieved 2026-08-22). Cited as the source for the tool-calling model used across this site.", "Internal editorial charter — this site."] },
      { type: "h2", text: "Last reviewed" },
      { type: "ul", items: ["Page last reviewed: 2026-08-22", "Next scheduled review: 2027-02-22", "Reviewer: BestAIAgent.in editorial board"] },
    ]
  },
  "corrections": {
    title: "Corrections and Version History",
    description: "How BestAIAgent.in records content corrections: correction log, severity classes, retraction policy, and the difference between refresh and correction.",
    blocks: [
      { type: "p", text: "Mistakes happen. The integrity of this site depends on how we record and correct them. This page documents the correction log format, severity classes, and the difference between a correction, a refresh, and a retraction." },
      { type: "h2", text: "What a correction is" },
      { type: "p", text: "A correction is a published change to a claim that was incorrect when published. Corrections are surfaced on the affected page with a visible \"Correction\" note that links to the entry in this log." },
      { type: "p", text: "A correction is not the same as:" },
      { type: "ul", items: ["**Refresh** — re-verifying claims whose evidence aged past \`expiresAt\`. The claim may still be correct; we are checking.", "**Update** — expanding the page with new evidence or context.", "**Retraction** — withdrawing a page entirely because its central claim cannot be supported."] },
      { type: "h2", text: "Severity classes" },
      { type: "p", text: "We use three severity classes for corrections:" },
      { type: "table", rows: [["Class", "When", "Page treatment"], ["**Minor**", "Typographical error, broken link, formatting issue", "In-page note, log entry"], ["**Material**", "A claim was wrong or out of date but the page's overall conclusion holds", "In-page banner, log entry, optional \`lastReviewed\` reset"], ["**Substantive**", "The page's conclusion no longer holds, or the page is unsafe to use", "Page moves to \`refresh_required\` or \`rejected\`, retraction notice on the index"]] },
      { type: "h2", text: "Correction log format" },
      { type: "p", text: "Each entry in this log includes:" },
      { type: "ul", items: ["Affected page slug", "Date of correction", "Severity class", "Brief description of the change", "Receipt that prompted the correction", "Reviewer name"] },
      { type: "h2", text: "Current correction log" },
      { type: "table", rows: [["Date", "Page", "Severity", "Description", "Receipt"], ["2026-08-22", "Multiple", "—", "Initial publication of the corrections log", "Internal — \`src/content/registry/content-registry.ts\`"]] },
      { type: "p", text: "We have no prior corrections to report. New corrections will be appended below this line." },
      { type: "h2", text: "How to report a suspected error" },
      { type: "p", text: "Send corrections, supporting evidence, and the URL of the affected page to the address listed on [](/about). We aim to triage submissions within 7 calendar days and to publish either a correction entry or a written explanation of why we declined to correct." },
      { type: "h2", text: "Related methodology pages" },
      { type: "ul", items: ["[Editorial methodology](/trust/editorial-methodology)", "[Evidence methodology](/trust/evidence-methodology)", "[Source classification](/trust/source-classification)", "[Author / reviewer policy](/trust/author-reviewer-policy)", "[Freshness policy](/trust/freshness-policy)"] },
      { type: "h2", text: "Source receipts" },
      { type: "ul", items: ["Internal — \`src/content/registry/content-registry.ts\` (\`lifecycleStatus\` field, retrieved 2026-08-22). The lifecycle state machine that drives the \`refresh_required\` and \`rejected\` transitions referenced in this page.", "Internal — \`src/content/registry/evidence-ledger.ts\` (\`EvidenceClaim.status\` field, retrieved 2026-08-22). The claim status (\`active\`, \`expired\`, \`contradicted\`, \`superseded\`) that distinguishes a correction from a refresh."] },
      { type: "h2", text: "Last reviewed" },
      { type: "ul", items: ["Page last reviewed: 2026-08-22", "Next scheduled review: 2027-02-22", "Reviewer: BestAIAgent.in editorial board"] },
    ]
  },
  "author-reviewer-policy": {
    title: "Author and Reviewer Identification Policy",
    description: "How BestAIAgent.in identifies authors and reviewers on every published page, including pseudonymous authorship rules and reviewer requirements.",
    blocks: [
      { type: "p", text: "Every published page on BestAIAgent.in identifies an author (where named) and a reviewer (always named). This page documents the rules we apply." },
      { type: "h2", text: "What we publish on every page" },
      { type: "p", text: "Every published page includes:" },
      { type: "ul", items: ["**Author** — the writer's name, or \"BestAIAgent.in editorial team\" for unattributed pieces.", "**Reviewer** — the named reviewer who checked the page against [](/trust/editorial-methodology).", "**Last reviewed** — the ISO 8601 date the page was last reviewed for accuracy.", "**Next scheduled review** — the ISO 8601 date the next review is due."] },
      { type: "p", text: "The author and reviewer are recorded in the page frontmatter under \`author\`, \`reviewer\`, \`lastReviewed\`, and \`nextReviewDue\`." },
      { type: "h2", text: "Author identification rules" },
      { type: "ul", items: ["Authors who write under their real name must have a public bio on this site linking to their other work. Pseudonymous authors are permitted for personal-safety reasons but must be approved by the editorial board.", "Authors are responsible for the prose, the structure, and the accuracy of the claims they attribute to other people.", "Authors may not review their own pages. The reviewer is always a different person."] },
      { type: "h2", text: "Reviewer requirements" },
      { type: "p", text: "The reviewer:" },
      { type: "ul", items: ["Checks the page against [](/trust/editorial-methodology).", "Verifies that every material claim has a receipt in \`src/content/registry/evidence-ledger.ts\`.", "Verifies that no claim contradicts an existing receipt.", "Confirms that the methodology declared on the page matches the rules in [](/trust/comparison-methodology) or [](/trust/rating-methodology) where applicable.", "Adds their name to the page frontmatter before publication."] },
      { type: "p", text: "The reviewer is the editorial board for methodology pages and a domain specialist (or the editorial board if no specialist is available) for product pages." },
      { type: "h2", text: "When the reviewer is the editorial board" },
      { type: "p", text: "For methodology pages and pages with no product claim, the reviewer is the BestAIAgent.in editorial board. The board is identified on [](/about) and its decisions are public." },
      { type: "h2", text: "Why authorship and review are non-negotiable" },
      { type: "p", text: "Editorial transparency is not a stylistic preference; it is the foundation of trust on a research site. Three reasons we treat author and reviewer identification as mandatory:" },
      { type: "p", text: "1. **Accountability.** A named reviewer can be asked to defend a decision. An anonymous page cannot be held to account. 2. **Calibration.** Future reviewers can compare their verdict against prior reviewer decisions and identify drift. 3. **Audit.** When a correction is filed in [](/trust/corrections), the author and reviewer at the time of publication are recorded, so the chain of responsibility is recoverable." },
      { type: "h2", text: "Related methodology pages" },
      { type: "ul", items: ["[Editorial methodology](/trust/editorial-methodology)", "[Evidence methodology](/trust/evidence-methodology)", "[Rating methodology](/trust/rating-methodology)", "[Comparison methodology](/trust/comparison-methodology)", "[Corrections](/trust/corrections)"] },
      { type: "h2", text: "Source receipts" },
      { type: "ul", items: ["Internal — [Editorial methodology](/trust/editorial-methodology) (this site, retrieved 2026-08-22). The policy this page extends."] },
      { type: "h2", text: "Last reviewed" },
      { type: "ul", items: ["Page last reviewed: 2026-08-22", "Next scheduled review: 2027-02-22", "Reviewer: BestAIAgent.in editorial board"] },
    ]
  },

  "how-to-verify": {
    title: "How to Verify a Claim on BestAIAgent.in",
    description: "A practical, step-by-step guide to checking any claim on this site yourself, rather than taking a published field at face value.",
    blocks: [
      { type: "p", text: "Every other trust page on this site documents how we produce and gate content. This page is different: it's a walkthrough for you, the reader, on how to independently check whether a specific claim on a specific page actually holds up — in under a minute, using nothing but the page itself and its cited source." },
      { type: "h2", text: "Step 1: Find the receipt, not just the claim" },
      { type: "p", text: "On an entity page (an agent, model, framework or provider), look for the evidence block near the claim — it names a publisher, a retrieval date, and links to a primary source. If a field has no such block, it means the field is unknown by this site's own rule, not that the claim is unverified-but-true — treat it as genuinely unknown." },
      { type: "h2", text: "Step 2: Open the primary source directly" },
      { type: "p", text: "Click through to the linked source and read the passage yourself, rather than trusting our paraphrase of it. This matters most for anything volatile — price, plan limits, model version — since these can change after our retrieval date." },
      { type: "h2", text: "Step 3: Check the retrieval date against how fast the fact moves" },
      { type: "p", text: "A pricing fact retrieved 90 days ago is a different risk than an identity fact retrieved 90 days ago — see [](/trust/freshness-policy) for the specific re-verification windows we apply per claim type. If a page looks stale for its claim type, that's worth flagging as a correction rather than assuming it still holds." },
      { type: "h2", text: "Step 4: Distinguish a fact from an editorial judgment" },
      { type: "p", text: "A number with a citation is a fact. A recommendation, a \"best for X\" framing, or a comparative verdict is an editorial judgment built on top of facts — it should be labeled as such on the page. If a judgment reads like a fact with no methodology attached, that's a real defect worth reporting." },
      { type: "h2", text: "Step 5: Report what doesn't hold up" },
      { type: "p", text: "If a source doesn't say what the page claims it says, or the retrieval date is older than the freshness window for that claim type, use [](/trust/corrections) to report it with the specific field and the source you checked. This is the same reporting path a reviewer would use internally." },
      { type: "h2", text: "What verification does not mean" },
      { type: "ul", items: ["A verified identity does not mean every field on that entity's page is verified — verification is field-level, not whole-page.", "A primary source can still be wrong; verification confirms we cited it accurately, not that the source itself is infallible.", "An evidence-ready comparison does not mean a universal winner — see [](/trust/comparison-methodology) for what a comparison page does and doesn't assert."] },
      { type: "h2", text: "Related methodology pages" },
      { type: "ul", items: ["[Evidence methodology](/trust/evidence-methodology)", "[Source classification](/trust/source-classification)", "[Freshness policy](/trust/freshness-policy)", "[Corrections](/trust/corrections)", "[Rating methodology](/trust/rating-methodology)"] },
      { type: "h2", text: "Source receipts" },
      { type: "ul", items: ["Internal — [Evidence methodology](/trust/evidence-methodology) (this site, retrieved 2026-08-29). The receipt structure this page teaches readers to check."] },
      { type: "h2", text: "Last reviewed" },
      { type: "ul", items: ["Page last reviewed: 2026-08-29", "Next scheduled review: 2027-02-28", "Reviewer: BestAIAgent.in editorial board"] },
    ]
  },
